# Line endings are declared here, not left to each clone's core.autocrlf.
#
#   * text      - treat the path as text unconditionally. "text=auto" is NOT
#                 enough: with core.autocrlf=true (the default of most Windows
#                 installs) git turns the AUTO branch into "check out as CRLF"
#                 and ignores eol=lf, so the very files this rule exists for
#                 would still come out with CRLF. Only an explicit "text"
#                 makes the result independent of the local configuration.
#   * eol=lf    - store and check out with LF on every platform.
#
# Because "text" is unconditional, every binary format in this repository is
# named below. Add a line here when a new one appears - an unnamed binary would
# be treated as text and corrupted.
#
# Why it matters: a shebang of "#!/bin/sh\r" fails on Linux with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M". rsync-backup.sh, e2e.sh, harness.sh, the mock-*
# helpers and both build-linux.sh are exactly that kind of file, and a Windows
# checkout used to rewrite them to CRLF without anyone noticing.
# postinst/prerm/postrm and the systemd unit are read verbatim by dpkg/systemd.
* text eol=lf

*.docx  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.gz    binary
*.zip   binary
*.xz    binary
*.7z    binary
*.bin   binary
*.so    binary
*.rknn  binary
*.rkllm binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4   binary
